BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      One day, a stranger appeared to the first village with a clay vessel. "Pour your water her) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        e," she said, "and it will flow to your neighbors threefold. But only if you trust them ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        to send some portion back.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      The villagers were afraid. If they sent their precious water and received nothing in retur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        n, they would perish. But the elders decided: "We must have faith. Abundance cannot grow) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (         from closed hands.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      They poured half their water into the vessel. It flowed across the valley and multiplied-t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        hree times what was sent now filled the second village's wells.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      The second village rejoiced. They faced a choice: keep everything, or honor the gift with ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        return? ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      Their wise woman spoke: "Those who sent water to strangers have shown great trust. To betr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        ay such faith would poison the spring itself. We must return generously, so the cycle co) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        ntinues.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
